4:T46a,The web doesn't wait, and neither should your business. After shipping more than fifty digital projects across the region, here are the five trends we believe deserve your attention in 2026.

**1. Mobile-first is now mobile-only.** For many of your customers, the phone is the only device. If your site frustrates on mobile, you don't exist. Design for the thumb, not just the eye.

**2. Speed is a feature.** Every second of load time costs conversions. Modern frameworks make sub-second loads achievable — there is no excuse anymore.

**3. AI-assisted content, human-edited.** Teams that use AI to draft and humans to refine publish more, rank better, and sound more like themselves.

**4. Local SEO wins contracts.** "Near me" and city-based searches dominate commercial queries in East Africa. Structured local data is the cheapest marketing you'll ever do.

**5. Accessibility is table stakes.** Inclusive design widens your audience and increasingly protects you from legal risk. Semantic HTML and proper contrast are the new minimum standard.

Want a free assessment of where your site stands on these five? Get in touch.0:{"buildId":"B61NDWfo9xL3yvlGtD_AZ","rsc":["$","$1","c",{"children":[[["$","section",null,{"className":"bg-pixel-grid relative overflow-hidden bg-navy-800 py-16 lg:py-20","aria-labelledby":"news-hero","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"container-site relative flex flex-col items-center gap-6 text-center","children":[["$","h1",null,{"id":"news-hero","className":"font-heading text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white sm:text-5xl","children":"News & Insights"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"max-w-2xl text-base leading-relaxed text-navy-200 sm:text-lg","children":"Agency updates, engineering deep-dives, and practical insights for organizations building their digital presence."}]]}]}],["$","section",null,{"aria-labelledby":"news-list","className":"bg-white py-16 lg:py-20","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"container-site flex flex-col gap-10","children":[["$","h2",null,{"id":"news-list","className":"sr-only","children":"Article list"}],["$","$2",null,{"fallback":null,"children":["$","$L3",null,{"articles":[{"id":"cmur2a9h5000gn3s83fjhave6","title":"QASADAN Opens New Digital Lab in Mogadishu","slug":"qasadan-opens-new-digital-lab-mogadishu","excerpt":"Our new lab expands capacity for client projects and creates a training space for the next generation of Somali developers and designers.","content":"We are proud to announce the opening of the new QASADAN Digital Lab in Mogadishu. The 300-square-metre space brings our design, engineering, and support teams under one roof for the first time.\n\nThe lab is more than an office. It houses a usability testing room where real users interact with our products before launch, a dedicated QA station for device and browser testing, and a training area where we run our junior developer mentorship programme.\n\nFor our clients, the lab means faster turnaround, deeper quality assurance, and a place to workshop their digital strategy face to face. For our team, it represents a commitment to building world-class digital capability right here in Somalia.\n\nCome visit us — the coffee is always on.","coverImage":"https://yrnmyrthjwvstmzxkzwf.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/uploads/2026/10/67b434da-f35d-488b-bd42-e14b9f8615fe.webp","publishedAt":"$D2026-09-01T00:00:00.000Z","category":{"id":"cmur2a8o3000bn3s8wg2m1b5e","name":"Agency Updates","slug":"agency-updates"}},{"id":"cmur2a9sr000in3s852u3nvv4","title":"5 Web Trends East African Businesses Can't Ignore in 2026","slug":"5-web-trends-east-african-businesses-2026","excerpt":"From mobile-first mandates to AI-assisted content, the web is changing fast. Here are the five shifts we see mattering most for businesses in our region.","content":"$4","coverImage":"https://yrnmyrthjwvstmzxkzwf.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/uploads/2026/10/b35d7194-fd7e-4b62-897c-fdcec8c1626b.webp","publishedAt":"$D2026-08-18T00:00:00.000Z","category":{"id":"cmur2a9bb000en3s86uaz3ykb","name":"Industry Insights","slug":"industry-insights"}},{"id":"cmur2a9yl000kn3s831nnww9s","title":"How We Built Al-Huda School's Online Admissions Journey","slug":"how-we-built-al-huda-admissions","excerpt":"A behind-the-scenes look at the research, design, and engineering behind one of our most impactful education projects.","content":"When Al-Huda Primary & Secondary School approached us, their admission season was chaos: phone calls, paper forms, and parents queuing at the front office. Here is how we turned that into a calm, digital journey.\n\n**Research first.** We interviewed parents, teachers, and administrators before designing anything. The insight that shaped everything: most parents browse exclusively on inexpensive Android phones, often on 3G. Performance wasn't a nice-to-have — it was the product.\n\n**Designing the journey.** We mapped the admission funnel from first question to submitted application, removing every step that didn't earn its place. The final flow asks only for what the school genuinely needs.\n\n**Building for reality.** The site ships as a static-first Next.js application with aggressive image optimization, so it loads in under two seconds even on modest connections.\n\nThe result: admission inquiries now arrive complete and organized, and the school front office finally breathes during registration season.","coverImage":"https://yrnmyrthjwvstmzxkzwf.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/uploads/2026/10/179ec087-efee-4e89-b45e-28a3b9a4e7a8.webp","publishedAt":"$D2026-05-05T00:00:00.000Z","category":{"id":"cmur2a8zp000cn3s8vhdkxqzn","name":"Web Development","slug":"web-development"}}],"categories":[{"id":"cmur2a8o3000bn3s8wg2m1b5e","name":"Agency Updates","slug":"agency-updates"},{"id":"cmur2a95i000dn3s82u5f80hi","name":"Design","slug":"design"},{"id":"cmur2a9bb000en3s86uaz3ykb","name":"Industry Insights","slug":"industry-insights"},{"id":"cmur2a8zp000cn3s8vhdkxqzn","name":"Web Development","slug":"web-development"}]}]}]]}]}]],["$L5"],"$L6"]}],"loading":null,"isPartial":false}
